{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427544-character-creation-and-rule-issues","id":1427544,"title":"Character creation and rule issues","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-07T03:09:51-08:00","id":1427544,"title":"Character creation and rule issues","content":"Hi everyone,<br /> <br /> I know I post here alot, this community is very helpful with issues lol<br /> <br /> One of my players is used to the dnd creation method of &quot;assign your highest number to your preferred stat&quot; you know lol 18 in strength or something.<br /> <br /> So he is trying get 5 dots in melee for a knife throwing assassin (I know right) I have explained to him that Min Maxxing isint the best thing for a character sheet as it leaves you with next to nothing with other stats and 5 in melee just gives you a better chance of success, you can't really one shot things with how the combat system works. <br /> <br /> &quot;This is how I want to make the character&quot; is the reply. <br /> <br /> Any advice on &quot;tackling&quot; an issue like this, as from what I have seen, being Meta is the wrong way to approach this game<br /> <br /> Thanks for reading","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26360-toa_kiril","name":"Toa_Kiril","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T03:11:20-08:00","id":1427545,"title":"","content":"Sorry. For rule issues he dislikes the messy critical and bestial failure possiblities, as to use his words.<br /> <br /> &quot;What's the point of making a character when I can lose points of advantage and mess the character up&quot;<br /> <br /> I have explained that it's a game of monsters but he is still unconvinced","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26360-toa_kiril","name":"Toa_Kiril","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T04:12:42-08:00","id":1427552,"title":"","content":"If your player is being hard headed about min-maxing, then just run your game and let them find out the hard way that being versatile is the better option. Alternatively just explain that Danny Trejo's character in Desperado didn't exactly win his combat against gun toting enemies, cool though he was.<br /> <br /> Also who does the Player think they will be hurling knives at? A thrown knife doesn't really cause that much damage against kindred, and against mortals while it can be lethal it just leaves evidence that you have to go find after tossing. Additionally how many knives is the Player wanting to carry and what quality are they? If they are hand crafted specialty items, they should be hesitant at tossing them randomly or if they are cheap mass produced internet throwing knives, then good luck finding ones that are actually balanced. From personal experience I can tell you that most knife tips won't hold up to the.....extremes of WoD combat situations, which means within a few throws, the weapons will be useless.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I have played Knife/Dagger specialists in Vampire before and they were fun to play, but it really came down to close in carving or surprise tackles, rather than ranged ambushes. For a movie reference try <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0269347/?ref_=nv_sr_srsg_3\" target=\"_blank\">The Hunted</a> with Tommy Lee Jones and Benicio Del Toro. A good knife fighter in Vampire opens up their targets rather that leaving the knife in the wound. While a vampire will more than likely heal the knife wounds, the fact that half their Blood Pool is dripping onto the floor tends to complicated their ability to fight.<br /> <br /> Failing that, just have one of the neutral NPCS be a Gargoyle, it is an undead block of stone, go ahead and try to poke it into submission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T04:43:14-08:00","id":1427561,"title":"","content":"If it hepls he's min maxing poorly for throwing knives. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You want Athletics for that. Honestly this sounds like a big problem cause hunger dice and be explained in a combat context as a risk reward system but it sounds like you want a social game while he's lloking for a combat game and unless the two of you are clear with each other about that this is going to end poorly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T05:24:06-08:00","id":1427568,"title":"","content":"With the blood dice he doesn't like the fact that his rolls have the chance of impacting his character. <br /> <br /> In dnd if the roll fails, the roll fails but in vampire if it fails it can hurt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26360-toa_kiril","name":"Toa_Kiril","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T09:04:11-08:00","id":1427599,"title":"","content":"I don't see any issue here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T09:05:36-08:00","id":1427600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toa_Kiril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427544-character-creation-and-rule-issues?p=1427568#post1427568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the blood dice he doesn't like the fact that his rolls have the chance of impacting his character. <br /> <br /> In dnd if the roll fails, the roll fails but in vampire if it fails it can hurt</div> </div> </div> </div>In v5 if the roll suceed it can turn into a fail, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T09:13:33-08:00","id":1427602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toa_Kiril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427544-character-creation-and-rule-issues?p=1427568#post1427568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the blood dice he doesn't like the fact that his rolls have the chance of impacting his character.<br /> <br /> In dnd if the roll fails, the roll fails but in vampire if it fails it can hurt</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's because he's looking at literally one single outcome of the potential for Hunger dice. And unless he's planning on ignoring stuff and running around at Hunger 5, Hunger 1-2 isn't going to regularly impact with Messies or Bestials, on average. A failure is a failure regardless, and things like Compulsions from a Bestial Failure can have interesting narrative and roleplay follow ups.<br /> <br /> it sounds like he's set on playing it D&amp;D style and really wanting to ignore the 'I am a monster' aspects of it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, you're using V5 based on talking about things like Hunger Dice. V5 doesn't do 'spend 1 for 1' points like that; it gives you specific arrays to spend, so you'd say, put 4 dots into Strength, etc. There's not a way to put 5 points into anything, as none of the arrays have a 5 to start with, just 4s as the highest ones to spend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 12-07-2020, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T09:16:30-08:00","id":1427603,"title":"","content":"Well part of the problem seems to be that the player doesn't seem to want to play VtM. Because the whole &quot;a bad roll affects your character&quot; is a fundamental component of the game.<br /> <br /> But I would actually disagree about having a wide spread being the betters strategy for a VtM character. Sure, you want a number of bases covered like enough Athletics to dodge attacks and enough Awareness to notice threats, but it's hard with the stat generation system to be so narrow-minded that you don't have anything to spare for those. But because of the nature of opposed rolls and the inconsistency of a pool, a &quot;jack of all trades&quot; character who has 2-4 dice in every single conceivable pool will barely ever actually succeed at anything they do. It's a far better strategy, and I would argue it also makes for a better group game, to have characters with great strengths and glaring weaknesses which are covered for by other Coterie members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T09:21:21-08:00","id":1427604,"title":"","content":"Well what's his set Priorities for his Character? If its in Skills (which Melee is housed at) then he has 13 points to input, no? Then its quite easy to set 5 points in from the 13 and still have 8 points left to put into other things in the Skill(s) column easily.<br /> <br /> Though as GM I would advise him that throwing objects is more attuned to Athletics than straight up Melee, so inform him of that before he finishes his character.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also remember that he has other two Priorities to set for the Ability columns; Secondary (9) and Tertiary (5). This should be more than enough for a decent spread, whilst still having a 5 in a particular ability that he's asking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 12-07-2020, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T12:39:38-08:00","id":1427621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427544-character-creation-and-rule-issues?p=1427602#post1427602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's because he's looking at literally one single outcome of the potential for Hunger dice. And unless he's planning on ignoring stuff and running around at Hunger 5, Hunger 1-2 isn't going to regularly impact with Messies or Bestials, on average. A failure is a failure regardless, and things like Compulsions from a Bestial Failure can have interesting narrative and roleplay follow ups.<br /> <br /> it sounds like he's set on playing it D&amp;D style and really wanting to ignore the 'I am a monster' aspects of it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, you're using V5 based on talking about things like Hunger Dice. V5 doesn't do 'spend 1 for 1' points like that; it gives you specific arrays to spend, so you'd say, put 4 dots into Strength, etc. There's not a way to put 5 points into anything, as none of the arrays have a 5 to start with, just 4s as the highest ones to spend.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have explained the different ways he can mitigate some failures, like will power re roll and Succeed At A Cost (i use this sparingly), when I talk to this player he brings up &quot;whats the point of making a character if the dice rolls can mess it up, i spent these advantage points this way and the dice get to take it away?&quot;<br /> He is the sort of player in games generally who likes making boss characters who cant be killed and can take on the world. The John Wick of games if you will.<br /> <br /> I was using 5 points as an example","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26360-toa_kiril","name":"Toa_Kiril","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T12:45:30-08:00","id":1427622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427544-character-creation-and-rule-issues?p=1427604#post1427604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well what's his set Priorities for his Character? If its in Skills (which Melee is housed at) then he has 13 points to input, no? Then its quite easy to set 5 points in from the 13 and still have 8 points left to put into other things in the Skill(s) column easily.<br /> <br /> Though as GM I would advise him that throwing objects is more attuned to Athletics than straight up Melee, so inform him of that before he finishes his character.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also remember that he has other two Priorities to set for the Ability columns; Secondary (9) and Tertiary (5). This should be more than enough for a decent spread, whilst still having a 5 in a particular ability that he's asking for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> this is v20 character creation isint it? I am playing 5E","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26360-toa_kiril","name":"Toa_Kiril","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T13:14:36-08:00","id":1427626,"title":"","content":"Ah, I'm not versed in that then. Also per what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1808\" data-vbnamecard=\"1808\">elmerg</a> said, since V5 creation mechanics go by set &quot;arrays&quot; already pre-set to distribute, he shouldn't be able to have anything in 5 via the limits of 5th Edition. None of the &quot;arrays&quot; go up to 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T13:32:18-08:00","id":1427627,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25523\" data-vbnamecard=\"25523\">Shakanaka</a> in 5E character creation, you can have up to 5 dots in strength. for example, which means that when constructing a dice pool around a strength based task, say punching someone with Strength + Brawl. 4 in strength and 3 in Brawl, for a DP of 7.<br /> <br /> If its not possible to have a 5 in strength or a 5 in Intelligence, why is there the option for a 5 point?<br /> <br /> you have set methods of distributing points: Specialist, Balanced and Jack Of All Trades but then you get to the age of your vampire and the ages grants XP to spend on your character sheet, if you chose an Ancillae and gains 35XP, they could easily obtain 5 in strength by spending 25 of those 35XP points","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26360-toa_kiril","name":"Toa_Kiril","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T13:48:54-08:00","id":1427630,"title":"","content":"In D&amp;D5E, when you assign stats, you don\u2019t get any stat higher than 15 (plus a race bonus of up to +2) at 1st level. You only get scores of 18 or higher when you level up and get more bonuses. <br /> <br /> When you play Vampire in it\u2019s 5th edition you begin play with a limited number of points to spend and, just like with D&amp;D, there is room for improvement with experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T14:17:39-08:00","id":1427632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toa_Kiril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427544-character-creation-and-rule-issues?p=1427627#post1427627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25523\" data-vbnamecard=\"25523\">Shakanaka</a> in 5E character creation, you can have up to 5 dots in strength. for example, which means that when constructing a dice pool around a strength based task, say punching someone with Strength + Brawl. 4 in strength and 3 in Brawl, for a DP of 7.<br /> <br /> If its not possible to have a 5 in strength or a 5 in Intelligence, why is there the option for a 5 point?<br /> <br /> you have set methods of distributing points: Specialist, Balanced and Jack Of All Trades but then you get to the age of your vampire and the ages grants XP to spend on your character sheet, if you chose an Ancillae and gains 35XP, they could easily obtain 5 in strength by spending 25 of those 35XP points</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> XP is outside the assumption of what he's doing, we were talking about just with the arrays themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T14:24:51-08:00","id":1427633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toa_Kiril</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">for example, which means that when constructing a dice pool around a strength based task, say punching someone with Strength + Brawl. 4 in strength and 3 in Brawl, for a DP of 7. If its not possible to have a 5 in strength or a 5 in Intelligence, why is there the option for a 5 point?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking about Abilities in regards to V5, not Attributes. I already know how the baseline Storyteller system works, barring the modifications added with V5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toa_Kiril</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">you have set methods of distributing points: Specialist, Balanced and Jack Of All Trades but then you get to the age of your vampire and the ages grants XP to spend on your character sheet, if you chose an Ancillae and gains 35XP, they could easily obtain 5 in strength by spending 25 of those 35XP points</div> </div> </div> </div>If in V5 your spread Abilities are already determined via &quot;Specialist, Balance, and Jack-Of-All-Trades&quot; and none of these said &quot;arrays&quot; start with a 5, then that's that to begin with. Or if he's at the stage of choosing his age and he gains the XP he needs- he can easily spend that &quot;25&quot; to just finish up getting the 5 in melee he needs by how your saying it. I actually fail to see what was the point of this thread if its that simple. By the time he gets to the stage of choosing his age for XP, all of his base Abilities would already be covered right? So how is it min-maxing to set aside the spare XP with age into a relevant skill in regards to his character?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T01:33:20-08:00","id":1427682,"title":"","content":"OP is playing V5 right? <br /> In V5, you need to minmax. Having an 'ordinary' dicepool of 4 will have you fail half the time for easy tasks. Anything less than 5 dice might as well be 0. <br /> <br /> If you're playing a different edition, Having 5 in an attribute and 5 in a skill might be a reason for embrace. It's fine, and you probably won't end up so weak with other stuff. <br /> Your player sound really new either way. 5 in an attribute or skill is a strong example of deminishing returns.<br /> <br /> Also 5 dots of melee for a 'knife wielding assassin' is... a little silly. You never want to get into an even knife fight where you can use your skills, because you'll both get cut up either way, you want to use a knife when your opponent is unarmed or unaware or a knight in heavy armour... you don't need five dots of knifing. If your opponent is gonna actually fight back with a weapon then you'll want a longer weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T02:39:07-08:00","id":1427685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toa_Kiril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427544-character-creation-and-rule-issues?p=1427621#post1427621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have explained the different ways he can mitigate some failures, like will power re roll and Succeed At A Cost (i use this sparingly), when I talk to this player he brings up &quot;whats the point of making a character if the dice rolls can mess it up, i spent these advantage points this way and the dice get to take it away?&quot;<br /> He is the sort of player in games generally who likes making boss characters who cant be killed and can take on the world. The John Wick of games if you will.<br /> <br /> I was using 5 points as an example</div> </div> </div> </div>Has this Player played RPGs before? Like DND or something?<br /> The way you describe him, I would say this is a classic Rule 0 type of thing. It sounds like he just does not like the concept of loosing in a game, which would render the whole argument stupid.<br /> If he has played other RPGs like DND or anything, he should be aware that even the best One-Trick-Pony can fail at his trick because all Systems use dice and most of them have a auto-fail mechanic. So if you have explained him all the imo fun stuff (messies, bestials, Succes at a cost, etc.) that benefits the Story and hes still like &quot;but I dont want to loose, like ever!&quot;, the problem would not be with the system but the player.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26305-takeochan","name":"TakeoChan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T03:03:50-08:00","id":1427688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427544-character-creation-and-rule-issues?p=1427682#post1427682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OP is playing V5 right?<br /> In V5, you need to minmax. Having an 'ordinary' dicepool of 4 will have you fail half the time for easy tasks. Anything less than 5 dice might as well be 0.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would half agree and half disagree with this sentiment. If we are talking about Contests (especially against other non humans), you need just as much min-maxing as your ST does (since their bad dicepools are as low as yours).<br /> For a fixed difficulty, it depends on your standards. With a dicepool of 4 you suceed easy tasks (DN 2) in about 2/3 of all cases which should be fine. If we\u00b4re talking natural dicepools (no bloodsurge), you should be fine most of the time.<br /> If it comes to those tasks that your Character has to shine in (Occult for Treme for example), you need some min-maxing, but even with a balanced skill array a pool of 8 is rather easy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26305-takeochan","name":"TakeoChan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T04:31:45-08:00","id":1427694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakeoChan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427544-character-creation-and-rule-issues?p=1427688#post1427688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would half agree and half disagree with this sentiment. If we are talking about Contests (especially against other non humans), you need just as much min-maxing as your ST does (since their bad dicepools are as low as yours).<br /> For a fixed difficulty, it depends on your standards. With a dicepool of 4 you suceed easy tasks (DN 2) in about 2/3 of all cases which should be fine. If we\u00b4re talking natural dicepools (no bloodsurge), you should be fine most of the time.<br /> If it comes to those tasks that your Character has to shine in (Occult for Treme for example), you need some min-maxing, but even with a balanced skill array a pool of 8 is rather easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he was referring to the slighly confusing wording of the difficulty chart in the core rule book, where it seems like 3 is the average difficulty.<br /> In the end the difficulty progession is pretty easily 'fixed', if one considers the 'taking half' rule. So the average pool of 4 dice is able to succeed at an easy task (while not being under considerable pressure) 100% of the time. Easily done. From there one can go upwards and define difficulties. This rule makes it pretty easy to visualize appropriate difficulties.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">&quot;Life's barely long enough to get good at one thing. So be careful what you get good at.&quot;</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26196-saturno","name":"Saturno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T04:46:47-08:00","id":1427695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toa_Kiril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427544-character-creation-and-rule-issues?p=1427621#post1427621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have explained the different ways he can mitigate some failures, like will power re roll and Succeed At A Cost (i use this sparingly), when I talk to this player he brings up &quot;whats the point of making a character if the dice rolls can mess it up, i spent these advantage points this way and the dice get to take it away?&quot;<br /> He is the sort of player in games generally who likes making boss characters who cant be killed and can take on the world. The John Wick of games if you will.<br /> <br /> I was using 5 points as an example</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like your player might not have a long love relationship with VtM in prospect. I would suggest two things: 1. Talk with him about if this is the only conceivable way he can have fun with the game. 2. Talk with the other players, if they'd like to play this way.<br /> <br /> If you like to play 'super heroes in the night with an extra portion of badass badassery' then by all means do so. If you don't then he has to compromise or leave for another group. Sometimes people just want to do different things and one has to accept that.<br /> <br /> Concerning messy criticals: We treat them in a way that the lost background dots do regenerate after some time (and after the players dealt with some implications of it - not so much that it disturbs the flow of the game, but so that they often have to improvise, because their retainer/car/cash is temporarily lost).<br /> <br /> Concerning the min-maxing: That can be a valid playstyle, but I as a ST would nonetheless confront them with the logical implications of minmaxing. Just because they are minmaxed on combat and not on e.g. social interaction doesn't mean that noone confronts them socially. A social combat in elysium could be a hard thing for a minmaxed fighter. Of course it has to fit into the chronicle organically and I would suggest to take care that this doesn't feel like you as a ST were mentoring/punishing him as a player. Loss of trust is a bad thing between players and STs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">&quot;Life's barely long enough to get good at one thing. So be careful what you get good at.&quot;</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26196-saturno","name":"Saturno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T09:06:22-08:00","id":1427717,"title":"","content":"-Scores of 8 is perfectly achievable in V5 character creation. 8 dice is very elite. Specialities in V5 can bring that to 9 (or 10? Do specialities from attribute and ability both apply in this edition?) <br /> <br /> -In V5, &quot;Brute&quot; vampires suffer pretty badly from the new rules; physical disciplines are far less useful for combat till later levels. If you wanna win fights, either use people to fight for you, or mail people explosives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T11:57:48-08:00","id":1427733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427544-character-creation-and-rule-issues?p=1427717#post1427717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Scores of 8 is perfectly achievable in V5 character creation. 8 dice is very elite. Specialities in V5 can bring that to 9 (or 10? Do specialities from attribute and ability both apply in this edition?)<br /> <br /> -In V5, &quot;Brute&quot; vampires suffer pretty badly from the new rules; physical disciplines are far less useful for combat till later levels. If you wanna win fights, either use people to fight for you, or mail people explosives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, getting a dicepool up to 8 is rather easy, if its in your 'thing'. Attributes dont have specialities in V5, just skills. And only 1 Speciality can apply to any roll (p. 159 Core).<br /> <br /> I would disagree with the brute sentiment, but that would derail this thread, so we should leave it at that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26305-takeochan","name":"TakeoChan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T17:20:43-08:00","id":1427777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427544-character-creation-and-rule-issues?p=1427682#post1427682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OP is playing V5 right?<br /> In V5, you need to minmax. Having an 'ordinary' dicepool of 4 will have you fail half the time for easy tasks. Anything less than 5 dice might as well be 0.</div> </div> </div> </div>In V5, each dice has a 50% chance of success. An easy or \u2018Routine\u2019 task requires one successful result. If you have a dice pool of 4, that is a 93.75% chance of success, and a character with a dice pool that is double the Difficulty can have an automatic success anyway.<br /> <br /> What on Earth are you talking about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-13T13:55:27-08:00","id":1428300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427544-character-creation-and-rule-issues?p=1427602#post1427602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's because he's looking at literally one single outcome of the potential for Hunger dice. And unless he's planning on ignoring stuff and running around at Hunger 5, Hunger 1-2 isn't going to regularly impact with Messies or Bestials, on average. A failure is a failure regardless, and things like Compulsions from a Bestial Failure can have interesting narrative and roleplay follow ups.<br /> <br /> it sounds like he's set on playing it D&amp;D style and really wanting to ignore the 'I am a monster' aspects of it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, you're using V5 based on talking about things like Hunger Dice. V5 doesn't do 'spend 1 for 1' points like that; it gives you specific arrays to spend, so you'd say, put 4 dots into Strength, etc. There's not a way to put 5 points into anything, as none of the arrays have a 5 to start with, just 4s as the highest ones to spend.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have tried explaining this, but he doesn't like the idea of the dice &quot;ruining a crafted character&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;it sounds like he's set on playing it D&amp;D style and really wanting to ignore the 'I am a monster' aspects of it.&quot; thats exactly what he wants. He wants to play the game where the dice rolls dont affect his character. a game where if the dice roll fails, nothing happens.<br /> <br /> when i say 5 points, i meant that he always picks the highest age of vampire, so Childer, Neonate and Anchillae. He picks Anchillae because it gives 35XP bonus for him to spend on character stats (with that you could by the 5 in strength, that was a poor example on my part, sorry for that)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26360-toa_kiril","name":"Toa_Kiril","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T01:32:59-08:00","id":1428327,"title":"","content":"I thought you were all meant to play the same age category of kindred? So all Fledglings, all Neonates, or ask Ancillae.<br /> <br /> Honestly how do hunger dice ruin a crafted character? While they're arguably more likely to trigger than they should be, they're unlikely to be so disastrous as to destroy dots in Advantages, and a ST can always refund the XP if it does happen. Loading control of your character for a few moments of game time is a concern.<br /> <br /> More I've played several games where a bad roll can have negative consequences, even D&amp;D, and it's more interesting than sitting around waiting for something to succeed. But I've got no idea how to explain that to what sounds like a risk-adverse child of modern D&amp;D errors never had to risk an elf exploding due to potion mixing. Compared to dragging around a broken leg for multiple sessions Hunger Dice are nothing (and you can always feed multiple times a night anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T03:12:04-08:00","id":1428330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427544-character-creation-and-rule-issues?p=1428327#post1428327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought you were all meant to play the same age category of kindred? So all Fledglings, all Neonates, or ask Ancillae.<br /> <br /> Honestly how do hunger dice ruin a crafted character? While they're arguably more likely to trigger than they should be, they're unlikely to be so disastrous as to destroy dots in Advantages, and a ST can always refund the XP if it does happen. Loading control of your character for a few moments of game time is a concern.<br /> <br /> More I've played several games where a bad roll can have negative consequences, even D&amp;D, and it's more interesting than sitting around waiting for something to succeed. But I've got no idea how to explain that to what sounds like a risk-adverse child of modern D&amp;D errors never had to risk an elf exploding due to potion mixing. Compared to dragging around a broken leg for multiple sessions Hunger Dice are nothing (and you can always feed multiple times a night anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I read under Coterie Creation you can have a mix of any age of vampire. <br /> <br /> I don't think they do, I think it adds an exciting risk and reward factor to the character as does Convulsions. But he doesn't like the idea of trying to be stealthy (for example) rolling a critical success and ripping the door off its hinges. <br /> <br /> It stops you doing things for a bit, because you've got your mouthful, but you can feed as many times as you like as you said, depending on how much you want to feed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26360-toa_kiril","name":"Toa_Kiril","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T11:08:11-08:00","id":1428373,"title":"","content":"You can play with a mix of age, my table is doing it right now. It can be really fun, as one could be the Ancilla/old Neonate &quot;daddy&quot; and the others are fledgelings/young Neonates ( a bit like the dynamic of LA by night). <br /> <br /> I think what you realy need to explain to your Player is, that even with a messy critical, you can still succeed at your task. So even if hes ripping off the door at a stealth check, it should be at a point where he still has an advantage (he stalkes through the whole house but on the last door he rips it off and the guard behind it could make a check to see him coming before he can jump him). Messy Crits should be like the &quot;yes, but...&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26305-takeochan","name":"TakeoChan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T11:25:49-08:00","id":1428377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakeoChan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427544-character-creation-and-rule-issues?p=1428373#post1428373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think what you realy need to explain to your Player is, that even with a messy critical, you can still succeed at your task. So even if hes ripping off the door at a stealth check, it should be at a point where he still has an advantage (he stalkes through the whole house but on the last door he rips it off and the guard behind it could make a check to see him coming before he can jump him). Messy Crits should be like the &quot;yes, but...&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>thanks for the help dude, and what would you recommend about the Bestial Failures? its both he is fighting me on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26360-toa_kiril","name":"Toa_Kiril","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T11:48:32-08:00","id":1428380,"title":"","content":"Messy criticals are 'yes, but...' while bestial failures are 'no, and...' Notably as written they are supposed to change the way the character is supposed to act, and encourages this with a small penalty unless/until they act a certain way. From the way I read them, which is the Beast getting restless or wary of something and encouraging you to act in a certain way, whether it's good or bad can vary depending on the ST.<br /> <br /> If he's actually serious about the 'crafted character' part you could offer him the option to pick one Compulsion, or two if he's Caitiff, and every time he rolls a Bestial Failure he suffers either that one or his Clan Compulsion. But I'm not sure that would work, 'crafted character' sounds like it might be a disguise for 'power-gaming focused optimisation'*, in which case my view is that 'they're making a big deal about nothing, in most cases complusions should be things that don't derail the situation anyway.<br /> <br /> * As opposed to optimising for concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T14:17:59-08:00","id":1428391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakeoChan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427544-character-creation-and-rule-issues?p=1428373#post1428373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can play with a mix of age, my table is doing it right now. It can be really fun, as one could be the Ancilla/old Neonate &amp;quot;daddy&amp;quot; and the others are fledgelings/young Neonates ( a bit like the dynamic of LA by night). <br /> <br /> I think what you realy need to explain to your Player is, that even with a messy critical, you can still succeed at your task. So even if hes ripping off the door at a stealth check, it should be at a point where he still has an advantage (he stalkes through the whole house but on the last door he rips it off and the guard behind it could make a check to see him coming before he can jump him). Messy Crits should be like the &amp;quot;yes, but...&amp;quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Or a straight up &quot;no&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T14:22:07-08:00","id":1428394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427544-character-creation-and-rule-issues?p=1428327#post1428327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought you were all meant to play the same age category of kindred? So all Fledglings, all Neonates, or ask Ancillae.<br /> <br /> Honestly how do hunger dice ruin a crafted character? While they're arguably more likely to trigger than they should be, they're unlikely to be so disastrous as to destroy dots in Advantages, and a ST can always refund the XP if it does happen. Loading control of your character for a few moments of game time is a concern.<br /> <br /> More I've played several games where a bad roll can have negative consequences, even D&amp;D, and it's more interesting than sitting around waiting for something to succeed. But I've got no idea how to explain that to what sounds like a risk-adverse child of modern D&amp;D errors never had to risk an elf exploding due to potion mixing. Compared to dragging around a broken leg for multiple sessions Hunger Dice are nothing (and you can always feed multiple times a night anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div>No trash-talking modern D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T14:56:00-08:00","id":1428397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toa_Kiril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427544-character-creation-and-rule-issues?p=1428377#post1428377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> thanks for the help dude, and what would you recommend about the Bestial Failures? its both he is fighting me on</div> </div> </div> </div>As TwoDSix mentioned, Bestials are a &quot;no, and...&quot;. The thing about these mechanics as I have experienced them, dont go strictly RAW, do as is appropriate for the situation. A Messy can lead to a Compulsion (thats what my group is doing most of the time). That way he may sneak through the whole house undiscovered but is sooooooo annoyed/stressed out by the whole thing that he just lets off some steam on the guard behind the door (harm compulsion). Now its not a &quot;failing the task&quot; but a consequence after his task.<br /> For Bestials, depending on the situation, a compulsion is a good go to. In my experience its best to not just roll but to select the best for the situation and then roll on those options or even give your player the option to choose (you get harm or hunger). On physical tasks he could get more damage/ aggravated damage or fall in frenzy/R\u00f6tschreck. It at depends on the Situation. If you have a &quot;bad day&quot; and you get one messy/bestial after the other (we\u00b4ve all been there...) you could just choose to ignore them.<br /> Let him understand that messy/bestials are not tools of punishments but chances for better RP. Part of VtM is the beast and (like karma) its a bitch...<br /> <br /> for a short reference, the &quot;Levels of success&quot; would be:<br /> natural/clean Crit = HELL YEAH!<br /> messy crit = Yes, but...<br /> success = Yes<br /> failure = No<br /> bestial fail = No, and...<br /> total fail = F*** NO!<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> As TwoDSix also pointed out, Compulsion are no means to &quot;make your Player play as they should&quot;. He can just ignore it (which would be kind of a shit move but ok) with him suffering the penalty on all rolls not involved with his Compulsion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26305,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26305-takeochan","user":"TakeoChan","date":". 12-14-2020, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26305-takeochan","name":"TakeoChan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T15:01:06-08:00","id":1428398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427544-character-creation-and-rule-issues?p=1428391#post1428391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or a straight up &quot;no&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>granted, it can be a straight up no, but that feels really unsatisfying. In my group (at least until now) someone always had a good idea how to handle a messy/bestial","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26305-takeochan","name":"TakeoChan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T19:04:03-08:00","id":1428426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toa_Kiril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1427544-character-creation-and-rule-issues?p=1428300#post1428300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have tried explaining this, but he doesn't like the idea of the dice &quot;ruining a crafted character&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;it sounds like he's set on playing it D&amp;D style and really wanting to ignore the 'I am a monster' aspects of it.&quot; thats exactly what he wants. He wants to play the game where the dice rolls dont affect his character. a game where if the dice roll fails, nothing happens.<br /> <br /> when i say 5 points, i meant that he always picks the highest age of vampire, so Childer, Neonate and Anchillae. He picks Anchillae because it gives 35XP bonus for him to spend on character stats (with that you could by the 5 in strength, that was a poor example on my part, sorry for that)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You realize you, as the ST, have final say on that right? If you feel like he's power gaming or cheesing it, you can tell him not to take it. It's mean to be a group decision that fits the theme of the game, not 'I want this because it's The Best Option'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T06:28:34-08:00","id":1428462,"title":"","content":"I personally have no problem with a character, that is highly competent in a highly specfic area. If they want their vampire to be one of the best knife trowers in the world - So what?<br /> <br /> Otherwise give you player the book to read and ask them afterwards if they want to play this game. Many people want play an optimistic power fantasy, not a dark mirror that will eventually break.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T08:42:39-08:00","id":1428479,"title":"","content":"^issue is, it's impossible to create such a character at character creation. V5 can give you 9 dice, best in the world would require 11. I think that's the issue the storyteller is having? I'm kinda confused by this 'dnd roll' thing they're talking about. Personally I think 'knife master' doesn't suit my tastes (halberds/poleaxes for rule-of-cool, rifles for open war, sabres for quiet war, handguns for night-to-night unliving) but i'd allow the concept.<br /> <br /> But also in V5, a &quot;Dark mirror that will eventually break&quot; is the norm and the one playstyle the game is geared towards. Action extravaganza it is not; the combat rules are really designed to get fights out of the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 12-15-2020, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}